{"availability":"available","full":"leandergrech/rl-rocket-engine-control","name":"rl-rocket-engine-control","description":"Deep-RL control of liquid rocket engines, built on DLR's LUMEN Control Challenge: literature review, domain primer, a labelled LUMEN-like surrogate with PI, PPO and SAC baselines, and an in-browser Engine Lab with an animated test stand","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-30T16:07:47Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:31:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://leandergrech.github.io/rl-rocket-engine-control/","topics":["control-systems","dlr","gymnasium","lumen","mkdocs-material","ppo","reinforcement-learning","rocket-engine","sac","stable-baselines3","surrogate-model"],"demo":"https://leandergrech.github.io/rl-rocket-engine-control/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:25.086Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:25.086Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:25.086Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:25.086Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A personal literature review and codebase for deep reinforcement learning control of liquid-propellant rocket engines. It is anchored on the LUMEN Control Challenge from DLR's Institute of Space Propulsion. LUMEN is a 25 kN liquid-oxygen / methane expander-bleed engine fired at test bench P8.3 in Lampoldshausen. The task is to drive two turbine valves so that chamber pressure (thrust) and mixture ratio track a reference, with constraints respected, under model error and faults.","DLR's own SAC controller has done this on the real engine at 1.3 % mean error, zero-shot from simulation. The challenge promises a generalised simulator and an automatic evaluation service so others can try."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/leandergrech/rl-rocket-engine-control/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"86ccad41baff7071a9fe202fa97e76b7d66f9e139b68923397